              "message": "Templates: the code gate\n\nEvery change a coding agent makes in a git repository is proposed as a\npatch, reviewed as a diff in the desk, decided and signed by a person,\nand committed only then: the repository's hooks refuse a commit unless\nthe staged tree is an approved artefact applied to the commit's parent,\nadd the CHAP trailers to the message, and write the evidence beside the\ncommit as a note under refs/notes/chap, with the artefact as proposed\nand as approved, the signed decision as the chain holds it, the\nreviewer's keys and the chain head. verify.mjs checks a range of commits\nfrom the repository alone, including an override's operations and the\nreviewer's signature, or against the running gate, and a workflow runs\nit on pull requests. propose.mjs is the command an assistant such as\nClaude Code runs when a change is ready; AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md says so.\nThe built-in agent takes tasks.csv through the gate on a branch with\nthe model the environment names or with a scripted drafter, drafts again\nafter a rejection that asks for a revision, applies an override before\nit commits, and finds its tasks again on a restart. demo-repo.mjs makes\na repository to try it on, report.mjs prints what the gate recorded, and\nthe tests run the whole path in-process. The read API puts an override's\nrationale on the decision and the artefact under review on the task\nview.",
