              "message": "Templates: the desk rebuilt, and chap-analytics wired in\n\nThe desk is an application in one page served by both processes, the\nsame in every template: a queue of what waits for the reviewer and what\nwas decided, a review pane shaped by the artefact (a code change as a\ndiff with line numbers, file by file, each file editable whole with the\npatch written again from the edit; a message as a letter; anything else\nas JSON), approve, request changes and reject with a note and tags, an\noverride as an edit with a rationale, an activity view that reads the\nchain over a range with filters and earlier pages, an Insights view that\ncounts decisions, rates, time to a decision, agents, models, reviewers\nand the reviewers' own words, keyboard shortcuts, light and dark, and a\nlayout that folds on a narrow screen. diff.js parses a patch git wrote,\ncomputes a line diff by Myers' algorithm, and writes a file's section\nagain in the form git apply accepts, checked by round trips through git.\n\nanalytics.py, shipped with every template, reads the store with\nchap-analytics and writes the interactive report, the evaluation cases\nand a refinement page with the correction clusters ranked, the\nrejection notes and the briefs; the servers serve them under /analytics/\nand Insights links them. The code change artefact carries each text\nfile's content before and after beside the patch, within a size, so the\ndesk can edit files whole.",
