              "message": "Templates: team review rules, commits signed by the agent's key, a one-command demo, and code-aware insights\n\nThe code gate takes a review rule from chap.config.json. Under a rule\nthat needs more than one approval each round opens with review.request,\nso a round starts with no decisions and an approval of an earlier version\ndoes not count for the revised one; the desk offers no edit there, since\nan override settles a review with one reviewer's decision. The evidence\nnote carries every decision of the final round with the rule and who it\nwas addressed to, and checkNote, which the pre-commit hook and verify.mjs\nboth run, holds the signatures, the digests, an override's operations and\nthe rule to account. The agent's CHAP key, written in OpenSSH's format\nbeside the JWK, signs the commits the gate makes with git's SSH signing;\nverify.mjs checks that signature against the agent's key in the note,\nand --require-signed-commit fails a commit without it. install-hooks\npoints the repository's allowed signers at keys/allowed_signers, so git\nlog --show-signature names the agent.\n\ndemo.mjs runs the whole gate in one command: the key, the server, the\ndemo repository and the agent, with chap-analytics writing its pages\nevery minute where it is installed.\n\nThe read API lists tasks by several states and gives each task its\ndecision log from the chain, every round included. The desk's queue\ncounts a task as waiting for a reviewer until they have decided it in\nthe current round, shows the approvals so far under a quorum, and its\nactivity list says what each call did. Insights counts how often each\nmodel's work is accepted as written and which files reviewers edit or\nsend back, and report.mjs prints the same figures from the same code.\nanalytics.py keys a TypeScript coordinator's snapshot before handing it\nto chap-analytics, and adds the files reviewers edited to the refinement\npage; chap-analytics itself now reads that snapshot shape, with a test\nthat the two shapes project to the same tables.",
