              "message": "Templates: review an agent's branch commit by commit, and name the reviewer and the model on every governed commit\n\nAgents that commit on their own have their branch reviewed before it is\npushed. With review_at push, pre-commit lets an agent's commits through,\nand propose-branch.mjs proposes the commits a branch adds as one review.\nThe desk shows them in order, each with its message, author, files and\ndiff, marks the ones read, and asks before an approval with any unread.\nOn approval the branch is sealed: each commit is written again with the\nsame tree, author and message and the gate's trailers, signed with the\nagent's key, with one evidence note for the branch. A pre-push hook checks\nevery commit a push sends against what the remote itself lists, and\nrefuses part of an approved branch. The verifier holds each sealed commit\nto the commit the reviewers saw and its place in the branch, and the pull\nrequest check takes an approved branch whole. The command carries on when\nrun again: it waits, seals once approved, sends amended commits to a\nreview sent back, and pushes a branch sealed already.\n\nEvery governed commit names its approvers with Reviewed-by: Name <email>,\nfrom the trust policy or chap.config.json; CHAP-Reviewer gives the\nfingerprint of the key each approval verified against; and CHAP-Model\nnames the model that wrote the change, from --model, CHAP_MODEL or the\nbuilt-in agent's provider. The generator takes the reviewer's name and\nemail from git config, or from --human-name and --human-email, and takes\n--review-at.\n\nThe desk polls brief task lists and reads the task on show whole, draws a\nlarge file when it is opened, and keeps the page still under a dialog.\nnpm run report counts branches too.",
